h="master" change_id="I702870e6efe13dd1365eccd38deac45082fbe2eb" commit="dadccefbd3fbb77b86ab3f2929fcc527f4c737b1" commit_message="tast: Move files around.  Move the tast command from chromiumos/tast/cmd to chromiumos/cmd/tast, and move all other packages from chromiumos/tast/common/ to chromiumos/tast/.  BUG=chromium:791878 TEST=still builds CQ-DEPEND=I58fa9ef006f9a0976c370252ce29f1c23a8db724 CQ-DEPEND=I6c065c7a2a422b8a4ee3b5dd467928a5c01f533f  Change-Id: I702870e6efe13dd1365eccd38deac45082fbe2eb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/807842 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="807842" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/tast" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast" ref="refs/changes/42/807842/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6c065c7a2a422b8a4ee3b5dd467928a5c01f533f" commit="32eee7b8a0ff80509075f20bfbb9226b9d11b98b" commit_message="tast-*: Move files around.  Update the location of source code used by the tast-cmd, tast-common, tast-local-tests, and tast-remote-tests packages.  BUG=chromium:791878 TEST=packages build with FEATURES=test CQ-DEPEND=I702870e6efe13dd1365eccd38deac45082fbe2eb CQ-DEPEND=I58fa9ef006f9a0976c370252ce29f1c23a8db724 CQ-DEPEND=Ie4cbbcbf8a6e166f79325dc26ad227fdfbdc5b67  Change-Id: I6c065c7a2a422b8a4ee3b5dd467928a5c01f533f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/807753 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="12" gerrit_number="807753" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/53/807753/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="12"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8af96a3f9fc039a2ccd9ee33b2d80e2a90d4dd54" commit="90f2addaa819df0b1d0e7363357f97d144b68c3f" commit_message="libchromeos-ui: big_little USE flag spawns 2 raster threads  The big_little USE flag is used to set the default number of software raster threads on boards derived from chipset-rk3399. The number of raster threads has been incremented from 1 to 2 as using a single thread restricted performance unnecessarily.  The devices affected are Chromebooks Kevin and Bob.  This patch came out of a discussion here: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays/+/741583  BUG=chromium:791008 TEST=build for Kevin, check now has 2 CompositorTileWorker threads  Change-Id: I8af96a3f9fc039a2ccd9ee33b2d80e2a90d4dd54 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/808940 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Jonathan Wright &lt;jonathan.wright@arm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Reveman &lt;reveman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="808940" owner_email="jonathan.wright@arm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/40/808940/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib8361ca86773f5858e5ed7e36dbd9a3b23392445" commit="43fdb0194dc089ade00ba7bb2361214e4c0b425f" commit_message="pack_firmware: Parameterize FMAP area containing EC image  Unlike glados family, samus stores EC and PD images in separate FMAP areas 'EC_MAIN_A' and 'PD_MAIN_A'. Add an FMAP area parameter to _MergeRwEcFirmware() so we can handle the samus config.  BUG=b:69859657 BRANCH=None TEST=`emerge-samus chromeos-firmware-samus` w/ CROS_FIRMWARE_MAIN_RW_IMAGE populated, verify success. Also verify `emerge-chell chromeos-firmware-chell` still succeeds. Also pass unit and functional tests.  Change-Id: Ib8361ca86773f5858e5ed7e36dbd9a3b23392445 Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/804703 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="804703" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/03/804703/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I22cec6880ef56cc008bdfde9a456f756f25025c1" commit="c8bf1834b6c3b569928aba6860c7c59368836d3c" commit_message="CHROMIUM/FIXUP: drm/rockchip/mipi: keep runtime-PM on while touching GRF  In refactoring this driver in CL:780120 (commit 56a1c67ece3c &quot;FROMLIST: drm/rockchip: Add ROCKCHIP DW MIPI DSI controller driver&quot;) we changed the range in which we keep our power domain enabled. The bridge sub-driver holds it between mode-set and enable, but not before the &quot;glue&quot; driver is poking at the GRF registers.  So, we need to keep our own PM runtime reference too.  It feels like this should probably all go into .enable()/.disable() (and not .mode_set()/.disable()), especially given that upstream describes .mode_set() with this:    &quot;Drivers which need hardware to be running before they program the new    display mode (because they implement runtime PM) should not use this    hook, because the helper library calls it only once and not every    time the display pipeline is suspend using either DPMS or the new    &quot;ACTIVE&quot; property. Such drivers should instead move all their encoder    setup into the @enable callback.&quot;  This works OK on our 4.4 kernel, but might be an area to address longterm.  This being rolled into Rockchip's ongoing upstream work on the original &quot;FROMLIST&quot; patch. v6 is here: https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/10095109/  BUG=b:70201512 TEST=boot scarlet without USB (where our power domain would otherwise be      unused)  Change-Id: I22cec6880ef56cc008bdfde9a456f756f25025c1 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/810207 Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kristian H. Kristensen &lt;hoegsberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="810207" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/07/810207/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ie31f5e54a6408b72a161a0dba000d8f1a4a1e476" commit="5259a5e8b37911101f3274a60b44d42e2e455003" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: add rainier device tree  Rainier is a scarlet-derived board, therefore its first rev inherits from the scarlet dtsi. It uses an eDP as opposed to mipi and most of the additions are to account for that hardware departure.  BUG=chromium:776441 TEST=make kernel without errors  Change-Id: Ie31f5e54a6408b72a161a0dba000d8f1a4a1e476 Signed-off-by: Ege Mihmanli &lt;egemih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/757159 Commit-Ready: Ege Mihmanli &lt;egemih@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ege Mihmanli &lt;egemih@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="757159" owner_email="egemih@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="16" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/thi